# Generated from: specs/104-re-pin-vibeue-to-a-commit-that-compiles-on-ue-5-8-macos/requirements.md
Feature: VibeUE tracks its UE 5.8 branch 5-8

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Onboarding clones VibeUE from branch 5-8
    Given a fresh consumer project with Game.uproject and git available
    When onboarding installs VibeUE
    Then it clones https://github.com/kevinpbuckley/VibeUE.git at --depth 1 --branch 5-8 into Plugins/VibeUE
    And the vibeue step reports installed

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: The old pin is drift, and refresh moves to the 5-8 head
    Given Plugins/VibeUE is at bc7bc45c1e2025123778560f45c15d1f8e1be41d
    And origin branch 5-8 is at eabe83aba0708aeb79ce586f23684417d17cb852
    When onboarding runs without --refresh
    Then the vibeue step reports drift naming bc7bc45c1e20 and eabe83aba070
    When onboarding runs with --refresh
    Then it fetches origin 5-8 and checks out FETCH_HEAD
    And the vibeue step reports refreshed

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: A current or unverifiable checkout is left alone
    Given Plugins/VibeUE is at the origin 5-8 head
    When onboarding runs
    Then the vibeue step reports unchanged
    And when git ls-remote fails the vibeue step reports unchanged and says the 5-8 head could not be checked

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: The dogfood installer tracks branch 5-8
    Given scripts/install-vibeue.sh
    When its code is inspected
    Then a fresh clone uses --depth 1 --branch 5-8
    And an existing clone is fetched from origin 5-8 and switched or fast-forwarded to it

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: No VibeUE tag or commit pin remains
    Given the repository's src, scripts, skills, and docs trees
    When the toolchain guards scan them
    Then none contains v5.0-ue5.8, bc7bc45c1e2025123778560f45c15d1f8e1be41d, VIBEUE_TAG, or VIBEUE_COMMIT
